  "sourceFindings": [
    "boot.js6-7 requires mini-files before npm-require; npm-require6 independently requires mini-files through the same module cache",
    "mini-files.js1-24 registers getters, pathIsAbsolute is a const initialized at114, and its only imported modules are path/os",
    "runtime.js35-43 wraps Module.prototype.load and invokes unchanged Reify runSetters after the original load finishes",
    "Reify index.js141-154 registers getters while loaded=false; entry.js195-219 publishes their values on runSetters",
    "Engine loadModule inserted the cached module then bypassed module.load by calling the extension handler directly",
    "The direct handler bypass supplies a concrete source counterexample for completed-load publication; there is no observed per-require export object capture",
    "R11 negative package-config cache does not publish export values; no config-cache defect is established by this failure",
    "Independent frozen1 reading also confirms main.js enables runtime.js before boot.js; original load wrapper then runs setters after getter constants initialize"
  ],
